Example 5.6
Out of the following two coordination entities which is chiral (optically active)?
(a) cis-[CrCl_2(ox)_2]^{3-}
(b) trans-[CrCl_2(ox)_2]^{3-}
Solution
The two entities are represented as
\begin{array}{c|c}
 & & & & & & & & & & & & & & & & & & &
(a) cis - [CrCl_2(ox)_2]^{3-}
(b) trans - [CrCl_2(ox)_2]^{3-}
Out of the two, (a) cis - [CrCl_2(ox)_2]^{3-} is chiral (optically active).
